<p> Sharnga <q>(Sanskrit: शार्ङ्ग, romanized: Śārṅga)</q> also spelled as Saranga or Sharanga, is the celestial bow of the Hindu god Vishnu,[1] primarily associated with his avatar of Rama.[2] In South India, the Sharanga is also simply known as the Kodanda, literally meaning bow.[3] Rama is often praised as Kodandapani, the holder of the Kodanda. The attribute of the bow is also mentioned in the Vishnu Sahasranama.[4]

